 how that would all turn out so  in that sort of respect I really figured  it would be a nice conclusion to the  main streets but in a way it also turned  out to be a bit of a farewell of the  Main Street but yeah aside from that I  also wanted to work a little bit more  with some more contrasting colors on  this building I didn't have many blue  buildings specifically for the reason  because right now everything nearly  everything in the game is blue and I  wanted to avoid having too much blue but  I really figured in this case it would  be quite nice to have it just to make it  look a little bit more royal and even  have those little purple highlights  which I really wasn't sure about that's  actually a sign behind there - for me  the purple highlights on the top of the  walls but I'm actually quite happy with  how that one worked out as well so I may  want to combine those two pieces a  little bit more in the future like at  the moment they're like there are barely  any options to actually make colourful  buildings but I definitely think that  the best way to do so at some point in  time is definitely by using these signs  to get some different colors into your  buildings and over here as well I very  similar to the buildings which I have on  the corners of the plaza with the  fountain in the middle of it  I wanted to sink these arches a little  bit into the wall but not entirely so  they still stick out a little bit but  they don't seem like separate walls  either and the same sort of goes for the  pillars there  or Gio's place inside of the balcony  there and not actually on the very  corner of the grid so this is one of  those buildings which really has  different grids for the different pieces  which I think and this is also something  which I've discussed and forums and in  many chats as well I don't think I've  really said it in a video to explicitly  I really think the best potential and by  far the most flexible part of this  building system is the very fact that  you can have different grids for  different parts of buildings but also  different elements within one building  so say put all of the pillars on one  grid and all of the walls on another  grid because it's this very system which  may actually seem very limiting if you  just start the game actually find that  many people try to get used to building  things with just one grid per building  but I actually think the most flexible  and really the most freeform parts of  the entire building system is how you  can use different grids for different  parts just because you can put  everything in two directions and ways  that is so completely free but you still  have can some control over it because  you can still keep different parts that  you want in different grids or even move  those different parts or at once that  it's so useful and it's so flexible at  the same time which is really something  where I think this game is really  amazing I think one of the most  important parts probably as a game in  this genre to actually be able to cross  is to be able to attract both the  players who are quite casual and just  want to build some simple stuff and have  fun in the game much like just playing  rollercoaster tycoon but on the other  hand you also want to try to convince  players like me who are complete nerds  and shut themselves up in their room to  try to make realistic theme parks in  games to actually buy your game as well  and that's sort of like the two markets  which you somehow have to both  capitalize on which I think a feature  like this building system is actually  really good for it can be really simple  and easy to use if you want it to be but  it can also be so incredibly flexible  and I just wanted to quickly by the way  have some backstage areas over here as  well just to make it seem a little bit  more like a real-life theme park and  also to see if you can actually build  the backstage areas and I do have to say  I was actually really surprised that  frontier added those little air  conditioners and things like that you're  able to actually make the backstage  areas which is something which is  actually really cool to see because  obviously theme parks are completely  fake but you don't want your guests to  see that you sort of just put up the  facades literally and figuratively to  try to convince them that they're in  this sort of fantasy world of the theme  park but behind all that you still have  the machinery and it's really cool to  see that frontier actually edit that as  well anyway I still have two pictures  which are the only pictures that I still  have of the finished Main Street as a  sort of goodbye this is one picture of  the little city hall building I'm not  sure if I can you want to call it a city  hall or a courthouse but either one of  those things it's basically something  like that and then there's also this  picture of the other corner  I didn't save any pictures of anything  else yet I was really figuring I would  do that later on but alas I lost the  main street but that said I will still  continue to keep building on this park  and will definitely want to explore some  different themes and different styles in  the future videos and definitely won't  add one and the series here and if I  ever get back to the entrance of the  park I won't rebuild the main streets in  the shape that it was simply because I  think it's a it's a bit of a waste of  time really and there was only like 13  hours I would much rather put into it  try to see what else is possible in the  game and I have no idea yet what I'm  gonna do with it but something else  that's basically what I want to say I  guess anyway thanks for watching this  sort of one-off video and next time I'll  try to come back to your regularly  scheduled not deleted Park files so  thanks for watching and see you later
 

